{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-flavor-split-substrate","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:flavor-split-substrate","kind":"proposition","title":"Closed and factored forms of the substrate flavor split","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-pair-skein-mass-formula"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-flavor-split-substrate"],"tags":["flavor-split","u-d-splitting","substrate-only","no-fit","hecke-substrate-atoms","categorical-derivation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HadronicMass.flavor_split_substrate","text":"flavor-split-substrate.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:flavor-split-substrate\"></a><p><em>For every nonzero <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>,</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\frac{(q - 1)^2 \\, (1 - q^{-4})}{3}\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\frac{\\hbar_q^2 \\cdot h_q \\cdot [2]_q}{3},</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1}</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_q = q - q^{-1}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q + q^{-1}</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-split-substrate.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.4.14","page":"b/prop-flavor-split-substrate","qa":{"counts":{"pass":98,"fail":0,"warn":3,"na":19,"unknown":0,"stale":105},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.HadronicMass.flavor_split_substrate","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HadronicMass.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
